Aerie-Purpose: Make secure DNS (DNS over HTTPS) off by default, so no DoH provider is contacted until the user selects one.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/net/default_dns_over_https_config_source.cc (default value of the DoH mode pref)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Chromium defaults the mode to Automatic, which switches to a DoH provider when
the system resolver belongs to one. If the system resolver is Google Public
DNS, that contacts dns.google. Aerie keeps all providers selectable in
Settings; only the default changes.

--- a/chrome/browser/net/default_dns_over_https_config_source.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/net/default_dns_over_https_config_source.cc
@@ -27,9 +27,11 @@
   // result in reentrancy and mess up registration between this code and
   // NetworkService creation.
   if (set_up_pref_defaults) {
+    // Aerie: secure DNS is off until the user picks a mode. Automatic mode
+    // would upgrade to a DoH provider (Google Public DNS among them) by itself.
     local_state->SetDefaultPrefValue(prefs::kDnsOverHttpsMode,
                                      base::Value(SecureDnsConfig::ModeToString(
-                                         net::SecureDnsMode::kAutomatic)));
+                                         net::SecureDnsMode::kOff)));
   }
 }
 
